+ * BOTH HEAD DISCLOSURES PAINT A DRAWN EDGE ON ALL FOUR SIDES AND NO CSS BORDER (R6 L5; CH-71;
+ * pass-6 critic gap 3; LAWS P6 §E). The pass-6 row photographed the top band only, so a
+ * `clip-path` that erased the bottom edge — the side that meets the board — passed it ×2, and an
+ * edge at 40–50 % passed WebKit. The row is the chair's four-band probe (pass7/instruments/
+ * edge-bands.mjs), read in the page: each side is a strip 8px outside and 8px inside the sheet's
+ * box, photographed with the edge ON and OFF (`visibility: hidden` on the edge layer). A station
+ * is one column (top, bottom) or one row (left, right) of the middle 80 % of the side, and its
+ * value is the best contrast, over the strip's depth, of the ON pixel against the OFF pixel
+ * under it: the stroke against the ground it is painted on. A station that did not change reads
+ * 1.00 and counts. Every side must hold ≥ 8 stations and a core median ≥ 3.0 (§2.4's stroke
+ * floor). Both owner arms clear it: FULL 13–17, QUIET 4.3–5.6.
