+ *      dismisses it and reaches no cell under it (the tape clause is retired to 3C-4)
+ *   8  under reduce the open sheet has no transition left
+ *   9  THE HOSTAGE (pass-4 critic): three at the table, B walking at 4 steps a second, C moves
+ *      once; C's dot on A's open chart steps inside the settle window while B is still walking
+ *  10  A CLOSE IS A POSE (pass-4 critic): every visible frame of the fade still holds the chart
+ *      and the sheet's height, by Escape and by the mark; a planted unmount at the close is the
+ *      negative control in the same run
+ *  11  your ring and the room agree: after a mouse open and a tapped open (the seam's arm (b))
+ *      both draw you on your cell; after a keyed open, both draw you on none
+ *  12  THE THIN LAP (pass-4 critic): at 390×844 two at the table the sheet laps the board by ~4.6px,
+ *      and a tap 1–3px inside its bottom edge dismisses it and reaches no cell (it focused the cell
+ *      below, both engines, while the sheet answered no click of its own)
+ *  13  THE GHOST (pass-5 critic): three at the table, A's chart open, C's FIRST move pending when
+ *      B deals; 1.5 s on, A's chart draws nobody (the seeded arm is the in-run control). The
+ *      interleave is ASSERTED on the green run (pass-6 critic): a recorder on A stamps C's ring
+ *      arriving on A's cell 20 and the deal landing on A, and the deal lands after the arrival,
+ *      inside 700 ms of it, with C's move not yet drawn on A's chart
+ *  14  BOTH SIDES OF THE EDGE (pass-5 critic, the cure's price): taps 1–3px inside the sheet's
